WEBVTT

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.450
Oh, I envy you, Ichigo!

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:28.780
Indeed!

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:30.240
Eh? Why?

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.030
You’re going to the Park,
aren’t you?

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:37.410
And Aoyama-kun passes there everyday on his way home.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:38.800
H-H-How did you know that?

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.270
Rumor has it that you’re often
seen walking with him there...

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:46.340
Not often. Just sometimes.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.930
His fangirls are all envious.

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:53.280
Some of them are your seniors and they’re angry.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.970
W-What should I do?

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:59.230
Don’t worry about it! Whats important,
is how you guys feel about each other.

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:01.370
We’re supporting you all the way!

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.910
Moe! Miwa!

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:05.150
Momomiya-san!

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.160
Ah...

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.290
Aoyama-kun!

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.260
See you!

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:16.200
Don’t you have club activities today?

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.300
Yeah. Shall we go together?

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.420
Eh? Yahoo!

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.680
Hum? Just a second.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.000
Hello?

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.310
<i>Ichigo! Come to Café Mew Mew now.</i>

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:31.090
Eh? Right now?

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.550
<i>Yeah, right now.
Run as fast as you can!</i>

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:34.530
Geez!

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:36.200
What happened?

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.160
Sorry, I must go now.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:41.120
Okay.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.620
I’m so sorry.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:48.120
Ichigo-oneechan’s so angry.

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.420
I’m not angry!

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.170
My guess is her date
was ruined.

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:55.750
That’s the most probable explanation. She’s sulking.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:56.890
I feel sorry.

00:01:57.870 --> 00:01:59.510
I told you, I’m not angry!

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:03.430
I can see that.
I didn't know you’re so transparent.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.390
I’m sorry for being so
easy to read!!!

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:09.350
Well, what’s the urgency?

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:13.850
Actually, we have found something very
important about the Mew Aquas.

00:02:14.590 --> 00:02:18.010
Here, let me use this cake to explain it to you.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:18.860
Cake?

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:20.820
Please take a look at this cut out portion...

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.500
This represents the Tokyo stratum.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:30.440
The chestnut in the cake represents clay
soil, which is rarely found in the ground.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:36.260
We discovered that Mew Aqua is most likely to be found in areas such as these.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.260
What does that mean?

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:41.390
Here, let me explain with this mousse now.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:47.470
Suppose that this mousse is clay soil
and this strawberry is a Mew Aqua.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:54.230
Our analysis showed that clay soil provides
a protective shell around Mew Aqua

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:57.690
preserving it for a long time.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.510
Hmm...

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:05.080
(Note: The Kanto Plain is the plain where Tokyo is.)

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:05.080
Lumps of clays like these only exist in
the loamy layer of the Kanto Plain.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:08.540
In other words, you’ll find a Mew Aqua if you search there.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:12.130
Um... but Tokyo is so big.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:14.420
Is there a more precise location to start searching?

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.090
No idea.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.590
Eh?

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:22.900
I’m sorry. As the chestnuts are
invisible from the outside...

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:26.500
I can’t deduce where or how many Mew Aquas there are.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:33.230
But, considering how Retasu-san had reacted to the Mew Aqua under the ocean,

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:39.120
we hypothesize that your body will glow
when it interacts with a Mew Aqua.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:43.030
Eh? Did that happen?

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:47.410
In short, your body is
a Mew Aqua sensor.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:48.970
Look at this paper.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:51.690
Roads are mysteriously caving-in, one right after another.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:53.620
I don’t think they’re mere accidents.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:59.590
The enemy must have found a clue,
and is taking action.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:03.550
If that is true,
we have to hurry indeed.

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:10.140
Yes. As I said before, Mew Aqua is tremendously powerful.

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:13.480
If the enemy gets their hands on it
and abuses its power...

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:16.810
Mankind will be doomed.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:28.490
So, we have to race to find it first.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.540
That’s what I meant by “emergency”.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.500
That’s all.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.220
This sounds serious.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:42.630
We are currently executing the new operation.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:46.840
Specifics will be reported as soon
as more data is gathered.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:50.890
All right. You must not
disappoint me anymore.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:51.850
Yes, sir.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.380
How long are you going to hide that from Deep Blue?

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:04.980
Just for a while; we now know it’s
in the ground around Tokyo.

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.030
Are you sure?

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:10.240
Since our information is
reliable this time,

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:13.660
I have sent Chimera Animas that can sense the ore.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:14.750
Hmm...

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:18.210
As long as a Mew Aqua is under the grounds of Tokyo,

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.080
they will continue to dig
until they find it.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:22.570
However, we should deal with the girls.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:23.800
Hum.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.110
Since Chimera Mole is causing so much destruction,

00:05:27.110 --> 00:05:29.470
they must already know
what we’re doing.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.700
What shall we do then?

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:37.900
Distract their attention, by causing
greater commotion above ground.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:42.280
Remember what our other duty is:
to get rid of mankind.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.150
What’s that?

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.240
A cocoon.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:51.240
Deep Blue, I will disclose your identity
with the power of Mew Aqua!

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:01.750
Argh! This is terrible! I can’t believe this...

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:05.470
Ouch... Geez, I have blisters all over on my hands!

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:07.940
My body won’t glow
no matter how long I wait!

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.760
Alrighty, in that case,
I’m going to do this...

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:15.690
Mew Mew Strawberry METAMORPHO-SE!

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.190
Okay, I will...

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:32.320
Reborn Strawberry Surprise!

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.880
NOOO! I hate this!

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:47.380
Ichigo?

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.900
Oh? Phew, it’s a dream.

00:06:57.890 --> 00:06:58.810
Sensei?

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:03.190
Miss Momomiya! Don’t sleep and scream in class!

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:05.690
I-I am sorry.

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.780
Keiichirou, that is...

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:16.200
Yes, this is the one we unearthed
at the archaeological site.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:18.330
Do you think it’ll work?

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:19.460
Not sure.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:37.700
Uh-huh, this is a good place.

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:40.290
Isn’t that cocoon getting bigger?

00:07:40.290 --> 00:07:42.370
Yeah, its growing.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:45.830
An adult moth will come out
in a couple of days.

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:47.200
An adult moth?

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:52.620
It has high levels of pollutants
in its body.

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:58.620
When the adult moth hatches, the pollutants will be carried by the wind,

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:02.080
and spread through Tokyo in a few hours.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.580
Mankind will be eliminated.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.510
Wonderful!

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:22.450
How about you?

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:24.020
Not at all.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:26.770
I didn’t find anything in my area, either.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.730
Will my body really glow?

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.990
I’m wondering that too.
But what else...

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:32.830
We’re not going to accomplish anything this way.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:34.570
Shirogane?!

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:36.570
I thought so.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:41.080
Hey, how far should I approach it before my body glow?

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.060
No idea. Go on doing
what you’re doing.

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.080
Eh?

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:47.230
Can’t be helped.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:55.340
Masha, return to the lab, and ask Keiichirou
to try to narrow down the search area.

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.770
Understood. I will go, I will go.

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:02.810
We don’t have any time left.
Let’s continue!

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:09.780
Alien! Alien!

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.320
Near! Near!

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:21.790
A bird’s nest. A bird’s nest.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:29.880
I was wrong. I was tired. But I won’t complain.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:56.660
Argh, look at the time!

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:58.990
Maybe they left without me...

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:01.870
Geez, why should I do this
day after day!

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:05.550
Well, I should. We have to find the
Mew Aqua no matter what.

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:13.760
A-Aoyama-kun?

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:14.720
Ichigo!

00:10:17.150 --> 00:10:18.110
Are you going home now?

00:10:18.110 --> 00:10:21.410
Yeah, but...

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:23.180
Sorry... I’m in hurry.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.680
You’re always busy lately.

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.190
Eh?

00:10:38.410 --> 00:10:41.660
Could it be that...
you were waiting for me?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:45.130
I don’t know what the situation is, but
you’ve been really busy, haven’t you?

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:46.850
Helping that shop?

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:50.170
Er, um, sort of.

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:54.630
You look pale. You’re a bit tired, aren’t you?

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.650
Uhm, I am?

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:58.820
Sorry for keeping you.

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:01.200
Nope, see you!

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:12.230
Too bad... and after Aoyama-kun kindly waited for me...

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:16.590
We’re not going to find the Mew Aqua at this rate.

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:19.470
Don’t give up. Don’t be impatient!

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:22.720
All we can do now is keep searching.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.620
You guys have some free-time anyways, right?

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.200
Free-time?

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:29.150
Yeah. I know you have nothing to do anyways.

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:31.400
<i>“You have nothing to do anyways.”</i>

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:32.780
<i>“nothing to do...”</i>

00:11:33.180 --> 00:11:34.320
<i>“nothing to do...”</i>

00:11:38.020 --> 00:11:40.300
I have things to do you know!

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:43.200
Even though he’s busy,
he was waiting for me today!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:47.240
While I go looking for the Mew Aqua in vain!

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:50.060
The other girls are here too, they’re sacrificing their personal time as well.

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:55.880
Oh, she’s snapped.

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:58.750
Maybe she hasn’t had a date with
Aoyama-san for a long time.

00:11:58.750 --> 00:12:02.590
Shirogane-oniichan hit on
a touchy subject!

00:12:02.590 --> 00:12:05.890
“He was waiting”? Aah, that Ao-something.

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:08.430
Don’t call him that!

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:11.720
Since you say Tokyo is in danger. I’m working hard looking for the Mew Aqua,

00:12:11.720 --> 00:12:15.110
without even seeing my boyfriend!

00:12:15.740 --> 00:12:18.250
How can you say I have “nothing to do”?

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:21.980
It’s our duty. Can’t be helped.

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:26.680
I know! But, I’m angry at your attitude.

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.720
Geez. I hate you.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:31.900
Ichigo-san!

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:36.560
Ryou, you’ve gone too far.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:41.400
Ichigo-san is tired.
It’s not Shirogane-san’s fault.

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:44.800
Again you’re speaking for Ryou!

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:47.160
I-I don’t mean to...

00:12:47.590 --> 00:12:50.140
Phew, what a bother.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:55.390
Hey, Pie!

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:56.440
Yes?

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:59.090
Quiche is acting strange, isn’t he?

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:04.360
He’s too aggressive in this operation, that’s for sure.

00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:06.800
I think he has an agenda.

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:08.860
Well, let him try.

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:11.770
I am not going to do anything
without reliable information.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:13.230
Hrmph!

00:13:24.170 --> 00:13:30.440
Oh, It was a beautiful day like today, when
I went on my first date with Aoyama-kun.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:36.430
Shirogane is the Knight in Blue, isn’t he?

00:13:36.430 --> 00:13:39.410
If so, how could he say such rude things to me?

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:41.630
I’m getting confused.

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:43.400
Ichigo!

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:46.030
Leave me alone, I’m busy thinking...

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:48.890
Am I interrupting?

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:50.320
Aoyama-kun!?

00:13:50.320 --> 00:13:52.890
Err, well, how embarrassing!

00:13:56.990 --> 00:13:59.020
Aaah, I’m going to faint..

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.010
Come on!

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:05.430
Ichigo! Ichigo!

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:17.440
Um, er, I just felt dizzy,
I’m fine now.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.830
You must be sick.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:21.900
<i>Aoyama-kun?</i>

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:23.020
<i>What’s this?</i>

00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:24.460
<i>It’s that girl again!</i>

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:27.570
Well, please!

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:30.570
No! You look pale, I can’t let you go.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:32.220
But...

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:38.310
The doctor is out?

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:40.250
Um, yeah.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:46.900
Eh? Eh? ...Aoyama-kun?

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:52.870
I can’t believe it! He’s going to k—

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:56.650
—kiss me?

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:08.200
Well? ...You don’t have a fever.

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:10.840
Aah, a fever...

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:14.620
You better rest anyways.

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:15.850
Y-Yeah.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:20.080
Oh? Is this yours?

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:23.380
Thanks. I guess I dropped it.

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.440
I hope it’s not broken...

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.990
Yeah, fine! It works.

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:34.870
It’s the new song by Candy 5,
isn’t it? You like it?

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:39.380
Yeah. I like it. But you’re not interested
in these things, are you?

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:42.330
Well? I sort of like it too.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:46.230
Eh? Is he just saying it to be nice?

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:47.400
What happened?

00:15:47.400 --> 00:15:49.740
Sensei! She needs your help.

00:15:50.610 --> 00:15:52.280
Then, I’ll go now.

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:55.820
Ah... how silly I am!

00:15:55.820 --> 00:16:00.540
Aoyama-kun was very kind. I should
have said “Thank you” at least.

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:20.500
Thank...you...so...much!

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:29.620
Aoyama-kun made me feel better!

00:16:29.620 --> 00:16:32.220
He always gives me magical power nya~!

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:37.160
Shirogane, I’m sorry!

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:41.250
I’m afraid I was a bit harsh on you the other day. Sorry.

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:44.850
Maybe you were just too tired. It’s OK.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:46.610
Thank you.

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:51.800
Ichigo-oneechan has suddenly become cheerful!

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.510
Did something happen to her?

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:54.740
I don’t know.

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:57.810
Now! Let’s do our best to look for it!

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:02.810
Hello?

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:03.930
<i>This is Aoyama.</i>

00:17:03.930 --> 00:17:05.380
Aoyama-kun?!

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:07.630
What's up?

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:10.560
<i>Well... are you free today?</i>

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:13.070
Today? Today is...

00:17:13.610 --> 00:17:17.740
You guys, we’ll cut out of work early in the evening today!

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:19.100
Because we’re getting too tired now.

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:20.830
Shirogane...

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:24.060
Yeah, I’m free in the evening.

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:28.520
Great! Then I’ll be waiting for you
in the station plaza at 5.

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:31.520
Eh? Yes? At 5?

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:34.220
Hello? Hello?

00:17:35.550 --> 00:17:36.600
Oh.

00:17:37.930 --> 00:17:40.530
Well, that’s just as well;
she’ll be pleasantly surprised.

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:42.940
Hello? Hello?

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:46.390
Geez, it says no service.

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:47.540
Well, can’t be helped.

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:49.540
Shirogane?

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:52.030
OK, let’s go now.

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:04.420
What’s that light?

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:06.350
Possibly...

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.380
What’s up?

00:18:08.910 --> 00:18:11.290
We got a signal from
the Chimera Anima.

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:12.360
Probably...

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:17.410
Bingo!

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:19.470
Looks like it found a Mew Aqua.

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:21.200
How about your cocoon?

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.350
Don’t worry, just in time.

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:26.770
An adult moth will come out before the Chimera Anima reaches the Mew Aqua.

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:32.210
Now, I’ll go to Tokyo Tower.
I’ll leave the Mew Aqua to you two.

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:36.090
What?

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:37.720
Nothing.

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:40.970
Let’s begin the operation.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:45.540
After all, it’s impossible to locate the Mew Aqua.

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:50.480
Masha, what’s this luminary?

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:55.380
This is...

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:58.740
Masha, where did you get this luminous string?

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:00.990
A tall tower. A tall tower.

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:08.850
At the top of Tokyo Tower?

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:10.610
Something like a cocoon...?

00:19:11.600 --> 00:19:12.880
Don’t tell me!

00:19:15.690 --> 00:19:17.780
No reaction here either.

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:21.900
Let’s split up.
Retasu and I will go east.

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:24.990
I’ll go west with Zakuro-oneechan!

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:26.040
Okay.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:27.600
Just a second.

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:31.750
<i>This is Akasaka. Can you hear me?</i>

00:19:31.750 --> 00:19:32.600
What’s up?

00:19:33.890 --> 00:19:36.340
Would you go to another place now?

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:39.610
I am heading there right now,
let’s meet there.

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:41.630
<i>What happened?</i>

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:46.050
Masha found a highly toxic cocoon.

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:47.790
Eh? What does that mean?

00:19:48.390 --> 00:19:51.480
<i>Probably a Chimera Anima of an enormous moth.</i>

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:53.750
<i>I’m afraid that the adult moth will hatch today.</i>

00:19:54.270 --> 00:19:56.770
Stop it no matter what.

00:19:56.770 --> 00:20:00.260
If we fail, Tokyo will be destroyed.

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:05.540
What do you mean “destroyed”?

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:07.350
So where should we go?

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:09.430
Tokyo Tower.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.520
It’s showtime!

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:27.770
Ichigo, are you thinking of him again?

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:32.210
I’d like you to think of me only, at least
when you’re playing with me.

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:33.570
Who’d think of you!

00:20:33.570 --> 00:20:35.710
You always treat me so cold.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:40.620
Stop that! I have no time to be with you at all!

00:20:40.620 --> 00:20:44.640
Next: “Stop, Time! Overwhelmed
with Sentimental Feeling”

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:49.060
Aoyama-kun, wait for me. I will definitely come!

00:20:49.060 --> 00:20:53.070
Heh, I don’t like that. Ichigo is mine.
